# Starter Defaults

Cells with no starter code yet. Editing any of them should record the text it
had *before* the edit, so "Reset code" returns here. Each cell reports the
starter it is currently carrying.

A cell with an empty `+default` block (the auto-capture pattern):

```{javascript}
console.log("EMPTYDEFAULT original");
console.log("STARTER<EMPTYDEFAULT>|" + JSON.stringify(defaultSource));
```
```+default
```

A cell with no `+default` block at all:

```{javascript}
console.log("NODEFAULT original");
console.log("STARTER<NODEFAULT>|" + JSON.stringify(defaultSource));
```

An autorun cell with an empty `+default`: every edit re-runs it, so the
execute-time capture races the edit-time one.

```{javascript autorun}
console.log("AUTORUN original");
console.log("STARTER<AUTORUN>|" + JSON.stringify(defaultSource));
```
```+default
```
